<title>GERMANY: Kvaerner, Thyssen, Kloeckner to invest 1.4 bln DM.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner, Thyssen, Kloeckner to invest 1.4 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>MAGDEBURG, Germany 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Saxony Anhalt state said a consortium led by Kvaerner, Thyssen AG, Kloeckner and Altmark Industrie AG would invest 1.4 billion marks in a new cellulose factory near Stendal.  </p>
<p>Saxony Anhalt premier Reinhard Hoeppner and economics minister Klaus Schucht signed a letter of intent with the companies.</p>
<p>The pulp plant will be build on the Altmark industrial site and will employ 300 workers. Suppliers could employ an additional 700, the government said.</p>
<p>The plant will have an annual capacity of 500,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
